  "delivery": "This all looks correct and complete. All fixes are implemented within scope, with tests added alongside.\n\n## Delivery summary — Gate 1 fix round\n\n**Fixed all 5 findings + the source URI note, in the same owned files:**\n\n1. **UTF-8 CLI output** — `__main__.py` now reconfigures `sys.stdout`/`stderr` to UTF-8 in `main()`, unaffected by `PYTHONIOENCODING`. Added `CliUtf8OutputTests` that runs the real subprocess with `PYTHONIOENCODING=cp1252` and asserts the Japanese segment survives.\n2. **`--config` wiring** — `demo` gained an optional `--config` flag; `ProviderConfig.from_dict` (provider.py) now strictly validates before any output/provider call: rejects non-dict configs, unknown fields (names only, never values — protects credential-like fields), bad types, unsupported providers, and now unsupported models too (only `mock`/`mock-echo-1` allowed). Added an alternate-adapter stub test proving `TranslationAdapter` is a genuine swappable interface. README documents the flag.\n3. **records.py hardening** — bool `schema_version` now rejected; segment span length must equal `len(text)`; `pages:[None]` raises `RecordValidationError` (no raw `TypeError`); duplicate segment IDs/orders and duplicate page IDs/page numbers rejected. Fixed the hardcoded incorrect Japanese span in the unicode round-trip test.\n4. **`deterministic_id`** — now length-prefixes each part before hashing, eliminating the `a|b,c` vs `a,b|c` collision; added a regression test.\n5. **Usage log** — `UsageEvent` gained `token_usage` (default `\"not_metered\"`), `actual_charge` (default `\"not_metered\"`, never implies zero), and `estimated_cost_usd` (known synthetic estimate). Verified no source text leaks into the log.\n\nAlso made the synthetic source locator an absolute `file://` URI (`source_path.resolve().as_uri()`), independent of CLI working directory.\n\n**Files touched:** `scholarly_translation/records.py`, `store.py`, `provider.py`, `usage.py`, `__main__.py`, `tests/test_skeleton.py`, `README.md`. No scope beyond the fix contract; no store/schema redesign.\n\nAstra should run `python -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v` to confirm.",
